            <ArticleTitle>[Simultaneous coronary angioplasty and percutaneous mitral valvuloplasty: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>266-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with symptomatic pliable mitral stenosis and a significant lesion of the left coronary artery underwent combined interventional procedures during a single session. From the femoral approach a percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty was performed, with unsatisfactory results and necessitating stent implantation. Thereafter, mitral valve stenosis was relieved by percutaneous balloon valvotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
